    "answer": {
      "short": "$1,3,5,7$.",
      "worked": "An integer has a multiplicative inverse modulo 8 if and only if it is coprime to 8. Since $8=2^3$, precisely the odd integers in the list are coprime to 8. Therefore, the elements with multiplicative inverses are $1,3,5,7$.",
